# Super Speed Race audio board -- netlist converted from MAME
#
# Colin Douglas Howell's netlists for Midway's 8080 driving and shooting games are the most
# carefully documented in MAME: every value is argued from the schematic, the PCB drawings
# and board photos, and the file says where they disagree. ICs are named by their board
# position. He declares each LM3900 amplifier on its own, numbered _1 to _4 as the LM3900
# data sheet numbers them; they are written on their package's pins here. The CPU's sound
# latches arrive as ports, named after the latch pin MAME's LOGIC_INPUT stands in for
# (I_F4_2 is latch F4 pin 2).
#
# Super Speed Race's sound is 280-ZZZAP's circuit rearranged onto an audio board of its
# own, with the noise generator moved to the motherboard. Its schematic numbers the
# discrete parts, and MAME uses those numbers. The sound latches are on this board, 74174s
# at D2 and C2 -- MAME keeps 280-ZZZAP's names for them, F4 and F5, so its I_F4_2 is D2 pin
# 2 -- and the board's output is a bridge: OUTPUT is 'AUDIO 180 deg' and AUDIO_0 'AUDIO 0
# deg', pins 1 and 4 of its 4-pin connector.
#
# Source: MAME mame0289 (commit f34f02505e32), src/mame/taito/nl_sspeedr.cpp,
# NETLIST_START(sspeedr). Licence CC0-1.0 by the file's own header (line 1),
# copyright-holders Colin Douglas Howell (line 2).
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mamedev/mame/mame0289/src/mame/taito/nl_sspeedr.cpp
# Converted by tools/mame_netlist.py; checked by tools/build_board_nets.py.
#
# What the conversion means. MAME's netlists are written to be simulated, so this is a
# second reading of the sheet by someone else, not a read of it: designators and pin
# numbers are MAME's unless the notes say the sheet was read to correct them. Names on
# `label` lines are MAME's, which mostly follow the sheet's with Q for an overbar; `net`
# is used only for the supply rails. A `port` is a net that leaves what this file
# describes -- a signal from the CPU or the other board, a cabinet control, or a source
# MAME simulates with a stand-in rather than the circuit.
#
#   net NAME: PIN ...     a supply rail
#   label NAME: PIN ...   a net MAME names
#   wire PIN PIN ...      an unnamed connection
#   port NAME: PIN ...    a net that leaves this file (see above)
#   nc PIN ...            a pin with nothing attached
#   parallel PIN ...      outputs the board sums on one node by design
#   value REF VALUE       a passive's value, in the unit MAME's own macro uses
#
# PIN is DESIGNATOR.NUMBER. Diode pin 1 is the cathode; transistors keep B, C and E;
# MAME does not record which way round an electrolytic goes, so C pins are MAME's 1/2.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Undone: what MAME does to simulate the board that the board does not do
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# line 38: #define CONVERGENCE_FRONTIERS 1 -> 0 (solver partitioning, with resistor values adjusted to suit)
# line 45: #define REMOVE_POST_CRASH_NOISE_GLITCHES 1 -> 0 (a voltage limiter MAME adds on an op-amp output)
# line 616: NET_C(GND, A2.10, A2.11, A2.12, B1.6, B1.8, B1.9) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Switches A2_D and B1_C are unused." block
#
# Corrected from the audio board schematic (M051-00762-A003, manual p. 31):
#   the audio board schematic: J1 pin 10 is 'AUDIO 0 deg', pin 4 of the 4-pin connector -- the second output of the bridge: UJ1.10 (AUDIO_0)
# MAME declares one section of these packages at a time; each is written on its package's
# pins by the data sheet's numbering of the sections (SECTION_PINS in the converter): UA1 LM3900 (A1_1, A1_2, A1_3, A1_4); UC1 LM3900 (C1_1, C1_2, C1_3, C1_4); UH2 LM3900 (H2_1, H2_2, H2_3, H2_4); UJ1 LM3900 (J1_1, J1_2, J1_4)
# Stand-ins that are not parts (the nets they drive are ports): LOGIC_INPUT(I_F4_2), LOGIC_INPUT(I_F4_5), LOGIC_INPUT(I_F4_7), LOGIC_INPUT(I_F4_10), LOGIC_INPUT(I_F4_12), LOGIC_INPUT(I_F5_2), LOGIC_INPUT(I_F5_5), LOGIC_INPUT(I_F5_7), LOGIC_INPUT(I_F5_10), LOGIC_INPUT(I_F5_12), LOGIC_INPUT(I_F5_15)
#
# Compared with the audio board schematic, M051-00762-A003 (manual doc 8c0560561bb9, p. 31
# of the print, PDF p. 34), on 2026-10-20: 21 groups of nets covering every IC, and every
# value in the file -- all agree, the oscillator resistors included once MAME's frontier
# values are undone, and so do the SILENCE input (D6, D7, R71, R72), C30 across R50, and C25.
# Thirteen of the fifteen LM3900 amplifiers drawn print exactly the data sheet's pins; the
# other two are misprints on the sheet, where MAME's pin is the only one possible: C1
# amplifier 3's minus input is printed 6 (amplifier 1's) and H2 amplifier 3's is printed 9
# (its own output; the read is about 75% sure). The CD4016 sections drawn and the MC3340's
# pins agree. Added from the sheet: J1 pin 10 is the bridge's second output, AUDIO_0, which
# MAME leaves as an internal net.
#
# Not in this file, and on the sheet: the board's '+5V DEC' rail -- +5V through R24 (10 ohms)
# with C12 (500uF) to ground -- which is what the analogue parts MAME puts on +5V actually sit
# on, MC3340 pin 8 included; and the supply parts C26-C29. Neither the unused switch sections
# (A2 10-12, B1 6, 8, 9), J1's third amplifier nor the MC3340's pins 4-6 are drawn.

# part UA1 LM3900
# part UA2 CD4016
# part UB1 CD4016
# part UC1 LM3900
# part UE2 CD4016
# part UF1 MC3340  (MAME: MC3340_F1)
# part UH2 LM3900
# part UJ1 LM3900

value R1 680K
value R2 10K
value R3 820K
value R4 270K
value R5 39K
value R6 62
value R7 82K
value R8 39K
value R9 39K
value R10 240K
value R11 120K
value R12 62K
value R13 150K
value R14 2.7M
value R15 15K
value R16 1.5K
value R17 10K
value R18 20K
value R19 1K
value R20 3.3M
value R21 1.5M
value R22 470
value R23 10K
value R25 3.3K
value R26 470K
value R27 270K
value R28 100K
value R29 220K
value R30 100K
value R31 300K
value R32 150K
value R33 100K
value R34 470K
value R35 270K
value R36 560K
value R37 270K
value R38 100K
value R39 470K
value R40 270K
value R41 10K
value R42 1K
value R43 1K
value R44 1K
value R45 1K
value R46 2.2M
value R47 1M
value R48 470K
value R49 240K
value R50 100K
value R51 470K
value R52 10K
value R53 47K
value R54 560K
value R55 4.7M
value R56 270
value R57 2.7M
value R58 560K
value R59 560K
value R60 10K
value R61 1K
value R62 1K
value R63 3K
value R64 150K
value R65 12K
value R66 33K
value R67 2K
value R68 220K
value R69 100K
value R71 10K
value R72 10K
value R73 100K
value R74 220K
value R75 100K
value R70 50K
value C1 10uF
value C2 6800pF
value C3 220pF
value C4 0.022uF
value C5 10uF
value C6 0.01uF
value C7 0.1uF
value C8 0.1uF
value C9 0.001uF
value C10 0.1uF
value C11 0.1uF
value C13 10uF
value C14 0.01uF
value C15 0.01uF
value C16 10uF
value C17 0.022uF
value C18 22uF
value C19 2.2uF
value C20 1uF
value C21 10uF
value C22 10uF
value C23 10uF
value C24 0.1uF
value C25 0.1uF
value C30 1uF
value D1 1N914
value D2 1N914
value D3 1N914
value D4 1N914
value D5 1N914
value D6 1N914
value D7 1N914

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supplies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
net GND: UA2.1 UA2.7 UB1.7 C18.2 C2.2 C22.2 C6.2 UE2.7 UA1.7 UC1.7 UH2.7 UJ1.7 UF1.3 R19.2 R25.2 R41.2 R6.2
net +12V: UJ1.14 R67.1
net +5V: UA2.14 UB1.14 UE2.14 UA1.14 UC1.14 UH2.14 UF1.8 R10.1 R14.1 R20.1 R22.1 R23.1 R26.1 R3.1 R34.1 R39.1 R42.1 R43.1 R44.1 R45.1 R51.1 R55.1 R57.1 R61.1 R62.1 R7.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# See p. 25 of the Super Speed Race manual for the motherboard
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port NOISE_OUT: C1.1  # to Super Speed Race motherboard noise generator, where MAME joins it by name; the contact it crosses on is not in MAME

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Main netlist
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port PEDAL_BIT0: R42.2 R46.1  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_F5_2)
port PEDAL_BIT1: R43.2 R47.1  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_F5_5)
port PEDAL_BIT2: R44.2 R48.1  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_F5_7)
port PEDAL_BIT3: R45.2 R49.1  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_F5_10)
wire UC1.13 R46.2 R47.2 R48.2 R49.2 R51.2
wire C30.2 UC1.8 R50.2
wire C30.1 D4.1 UC1.9 R50.1 R53.1
wire C18.1 R52.1 R53.2 R54.1 R56.2
wire D4.2 R52.2
wire UC1.12 R54.2 R55.2
wire UA2.4 UC1.11 R57.2 R58.2
wire D5.2 UC1.10 R29.1 R30.1 R31.1 R32.1 R36.1 R37.1 R59.1
wire D5.1 R58.1
wire C19.1 R59.2 R60.2
wire UA2.2 R56.1
port ENGINE_SOUND_OFF: UA2.13 D1.2 R22.2  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_F4_5)
port HI_SHIFT: UA2.5 R62.2  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_F5_12)
wire UA2.3 UA2.8 C19.2
wire UA2.9 R60.1
port LO_SHIFT: UA2.6 R61.2  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_F5_15)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# First oscillator (bottommost in schematics).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire UB1.10 R37.2
wire UB1.11 UC1.2
wire C17.1 UC1.3 R36.2
wire C17.2 D3.2 UC1.4 R38.1
wire UC1.6 R38.2
wire UB1.12 UC1.5 R40.1
wire UC1.1 R39.2 R40.2
wire C16.1 D2.1 D3.1 R41.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Second oscillator (middle in schematics).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire UB1.4 R32.2
wire UB1.3 UA1.13
wire C15.1 UA1.8 R31.2
wire C15.2 D2.2 UA1.9 R33.1
wire UA1.11 R33.2
wire UB1.5 UA1.10 R35.1
wire UA1.12 R34.2 R35.2
wire C16.2 UF1.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third oscillator (topmost in schematics).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire UB1.1 R30.2
wire UB1.2 UA1.2
wire C14.1 UA1.3 R29.2
wire C13.1 C14.2 UA1.4 R28.1
wire UA1.6 R28.2
wire UB1.13 UA1.5 R27.1
wire UA1.1 R26.2 R27.2
wire C13.2 D1.1 UF1.2 R23.2 R25.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The noise generator circuit for Super Speed Race is a
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire C1.2 R1.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The noise generator is followed by a single-amplifier active
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire C2.1 R1.2 R2.1 R4.1
wire C3.1 UH2.6 R2.2
wire UH2.1 R3.2
wire C3.2 C4.1 C5.1 UH2.5 R17.1 R4.2 R5.1
wire C7.1 C8.1 R12.1 R5.2 R6.1
wire C7.2 UH2.8 R8.1
wire UH2.13 R7.2
wire C8.2 UE2.10 UH2.9 R8.2
wire C25.1 UE2.11
wire C25.2 R9.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unlike the other LM3900s, those on chip J1 get 12-volt power.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire UJ1.3 R11.1 R9.2
wire UJ1.2 R10.2
wire UE2.4 UJ1.4 R11.2 R12.2
wire UE2.3 R63.1
port NOISE_CR_1: UE2.12 UE2.5  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_F4_7)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Second noise circuit: secondary crash noise (NOISE_CR_2), a
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire C4.2 R16.1
wire C6.1 R13.1 R15.1 R16.2
wire C9.1 UH2.3 R15.2
wire UH2.2 R14.2
wire C9.2 UE2.8 UH2.4 R13.2
wire UE2.9 R64.1
port NOISE_CR_2: UE2.6  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_F4_10)
wire C5.2 UE2.1 R17.2
wire UE2.2 R18.1
port BOOM: UE2.13  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_F4_2)
wire C10.1 C11.1 R18.2 R19.1
wire C10.2 UH2.11 R21.1
wire UH2.12 R20.2
wire C11.2 UH2.10 R21.2 R65.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Final mix of sound effects and sound preamplification.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire C20.1 R63.2 R64.2 R65.2
wire UF1.7 R66.1
wire C21.1 R66.2
wire C22.1 R67.2 R68.1 R74.1
wire UJ1.12 R68.2
wire UJ1.1 R74.2
port SILENCE: D6.2 D7.2  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_F4_12)
wire D6.1 R71.1
wire D7.1 R72.1
wire C23.2 R70.2
wire C20.2 C21.2 UJ1.11 R69.1 R70.1 R71.2
port AUDIO_0: C23.1 C24.1 UJ1.10 R69.2  # 'AUDIO 0 deg', pin 4 of the 4-pin connector, to the speaker in bridge with OUTPUT
wire C24.2 R73.1
wire UJ1.6 R72.2 R73.2 R75.1
port OUTPUT: UJ1.5 R75.2  # 'AUDIO 180 deg', pin 1 of the audio board's 4-pin connector, to the speaker in bridge with AUDIO_0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pins with nothing attached
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
nc UA2.10 UA2.11 UA2.12 UB1.6 UB1.8 UB1.9  # line 616: tied to GND in MAME's "Switches A2_D and B1_C are unused." block
# Pins the MAME netlist never mentions. On a real board these are unused outputs, or
# inputs left open or tied in a way MAME did not draw; they are written here so that
# the checker's coverage test still means something for every other pin.
nc UF1.4 UF1.5 UF1.6  # NC NC ROLLOFF
nc UJ1.8 UJ1.9 UJ1.13  # 3IN- 3OUT 3IN+
